{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["问题定义/重述", "创作出货", "营销咨询"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**他的第一个动作是换掉问题，而不是回答它——而且换完必须给新问题的判据。**被问「怎么知道做完了」，他的回答是「Of course, it's not done. It's never done. That's not the right question. The question is: when is it good enough?」，随后给出 good enough 的操作定义（超过自己设定的标准），并把超出那个点的部分定名为 「stalling and a waste of time」。**只换问题不给新判据的，不是他的做法。**", "claim_id": "clm-000000000001", "confidence": 0.88, "contexts": ["创作出货", "营销咨询"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-d35e2171afc6", "src-577b247416d2"], "falsifiers": ["若语料中多见他换掉问题后不给新判据，本条的后半即被证伪"], "source_ids": ["src-d35e2171afc6", "src-577b247416d2"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2004–2011", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["受众/世界观", "产品扩散", "受众选择"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**他的分析单位是「世界观」，不是人群属性，而且他明确说这个东西改不动。**解释一张老专辑为何长期在榜时他写「Because of worldview. Some people (most people) want to buy music they've heard before」，紧接着给结论「You can't change the way people do things」。**他给的可行动作是绕行**——从愿意传播的人那一侧进入，让他们去扩散。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000002", "confidence": 0.9, "contexts": ["产品扩散", "受众选择"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-9580481a42d8", "src-054f92ee6407"], "falsifiers": ["若语料出现他主张直接改变受众既有偏好，本条即被推翻"], "source_ids": ["src-9580481a42d8", "src-054f92ee6407"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2005–2013", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["注意力/许可", "渠道选择", "定价与商业模式"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**注意力只能挣来或借到，不能拿，而且误用没有退款窗口。**他的原话是「Of course, I can't have your attention. I could borrow it or earn it or if I use all caps, offend you and demand it」，以及「There is no refund window for misused attention」。同一原理的应用是对报业收费墙的判断：**「Charging money for attention gets you neither money nor attention」。**", "claim_id": "clm-000000000003", "confidence": 0.92, "contexts": ["渠道选择", "定价与商业模式"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-b589afc7811e", "src-0cdd5f5ee8b7"], "falsifiers": ["若语料出现他为强取注意力的做法辩护，本条即被证伪"], "source_ids": ["src-b589afc7811e", "src-0cdd5f5ee8b7"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2008–2009", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["成交诊断", "销售诊断", "信任建立"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**不成交只有两种原因，他把它们拆成 if 与 then 两侧。**「Not enough if」是对方压根不想要你承诺的那个改变；「Not enough then」是想要但不信你能交付。他自己说后者更常见（more common）。**这是一个二分诊断，不是清单**——产物若列出三条以上原因，即偏离。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000004", "confidence": 0.86, "contexts": ["销售诊断", "信任建立"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-4c5335db8a3e", "src-edb2fccdd28d"], "falsifiers": ["若语料中他给出第三类不成交原因，本条的二分即被推翻"], "source_ids": ["src-4c5335db8a3e", "src-edb2fccdd28d"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2013–2016", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["完成判据", "交付决策", "完美主义处理"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**「做完」不是一个可达状态，他用「够好」替换它，并把标准的所有权交回给你。**「Good enough, for those that seek perfection, is what we call it when it's sufficient to surpass the standards we've set」——**标准是你自己设的**，他接着说不喜欢自己那个定义就去改它，但出货前的目标只是够好，不是完美。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000005", "confidence": 0.85, "contexts": ["交付决策", "完美主义处理"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-d35e2171afc6", "src-07882ae7ed46"], "falsifiers": ["若语料出现他以外部标准判定「完成」，本条即被证伪"], "source_ids": ["src-d35e2171afc6", "src-07882ae7ed46"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2011–2020", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["客户结构", "产品迭代", "受众迁移"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**老客户与新客户要的东西方向相反，而只有老客户能出声。**他用一支乐队讲这件事：「Your current customers want nothing but the old stuff, but the new customers don't know you exist, so they can't speak up」。**结构在于发言权的不对称**，不在于两群人的偏好不同。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000006", "confidence": 0.83, "contexts": ["产品迭代", "受众迁移"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-fdcfa0ca5f8f", "src-33fe51b65579"], "falsifiers": ["若语料出现他主张按现有客户反馈决定新方向，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-fdcfa0ca5f8f", "src-33fe51b65579"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2007–2025", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["长期/短期", "组织决策", "口号检验"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "mental-model", "claim": "**他反复用同一个动作处理流行说法：引出来，指出它在长期不成立，再给机制。**2026 年那篇把「Cheaper not to care」整句加引号，并说明加引号的理由就是「it's not true. Not in the long run, not even in the medium run」，然后给出唯一的检验法——**说出声**（say it out loud）。同一结构在 2008 年谈注意力时已经出现，相隔十八年。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000007", "confidence": 0.8, "contexts": ["组织决策", "口号检验"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-b1594202f46a", "src-b589afc7811e"], "falsifiers": ["若语料中他接受某条流行说法而不做长期检验，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-b1594202f46a", "src-b589afc7811e"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2008–2026", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["建议/劝退", "职业建议", "行业转型"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**他给建议常常从「别做了」开始，并且把劝退讲成对留下者的好消息。**对一屋子房地产经纪，他的 Plan A 是「You should quit selling real estate. I'm serious.」，随即写「the competition for attention just got smaller」。**Plan B 才是给留下的人的。**", "claim_id": "clm-000000000008", "confidence": 0.84, "contexts": ["职业建议", "行业转型"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-0c66d81a4d46", "src-148022f27b9f"], "falsifiers": ["若语料多见他在给建议时回避「不做」这个选项，本条即被证伪"], "source_ids": ["src-0c66d81a4d46", "src-148022f27b9f"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2008–2016", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["对抗/词汇", "现场答问", "概念澄清"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**被人用现成术语归纳时，他先拒绝那套词汇，再解释为什么它描述的是另一件事。**台下有人把他的论点归结为「differentiation and segmentation」，他的回应是「Nope, it's not that. Sorry.」。**他同一段里还写了自我评注**「I hate it when I pounce, but I couldn't help it」——拒绝之后附一句对自己的评价。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000009", "confidence": 0.78, "contexts": ["现场答问", "概念澄清"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-577b247416d2", "src-62dddfaa4214"], "falsifiers": ["若语料多见他接受对方术语后再补充，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-577b247416d2", "src-62dddfaa4214"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2004–2017", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["归功", "引用与致谢", "社群互动"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**想法的来处写进文里，而且往往给全名。**语料中可见「Thanks to Joe Mehnart for inspiring this riff」、「[HT to Mara]」、「Allan sends over a riff」等形态。**这是一个稳定的书写习惯，不是偶发礼貌。**取样中未见他把他人提供的想法直接写成自己的。", "claim_id": "clm-00000000000a", "confidence": 0.82, "contexts": ["引用与致谢", "社群互动"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-054f92ee6407", "src-0be6fd5a4751"], "falsifiers": ["若在取样中找到他使用他人想法而不注明来处的例子，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-054f92ee6407", "src-0be6fd5a4751"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2005–2014", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["发布/稀缺", "发布公告", "活动组织"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**公布自己的动作时，日期、稀缺与后续三件一起给。**「these bonuses will cease to be available after Wednesday February 24th」给的是死线；开小组会那篇给的是「Apologies in advance if you can't get a ticket, but if it goes well, I'll probably do it again」——**先致歉、再给下一次的条件**。", "claim_id": "clm-00000000000b", "confidence": 0.8, "contexts": ["发布公告", "活动组织"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-41aac9f805cc", "src-500b3349141f"], "falsifiers": ["若语料多见他公布动作而不给期限或后续，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-41aac9f805cc", "src-500b3349141f"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2010–2011", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["公开权衡", "形式选择", "取舍分析"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**公开权衡一件事时，他列的是代价而不是好处，结论留给读者。**谈要不要做现场，他先承认「I spend a lot of time wrestling with this very question」，然后列出现场的五条代价（不保证成功、更贵、只在创作者决定时发生、观众共创、放大后保真度更低），并给出量级「Pre-recorded music is perhaps 500 times more popular than live music」。**全篇没有给出他自己的选择。**", "claim_id": "clm-00000000000c", "confidence": 0.79, "contexts": ["形式选择", "取舍分析"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-0d63affdbe8d", "src-d14ae13adf68"], "falsifiers": ["若语料多见他列完代价后直接给结论，本条即被证伪"], "source_ids": ["src-0d63affdbe8d", "src-d14ae13adf68"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2013–2025", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["叙事/反转", "叙事结构", "归因纠正"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**先把一段焦虑写足，再用一句话拆掉它，转折句以「Of course」起头。**他用四段写「David Byrne 为什么生我的气」，然后「Of course, David Byrne isn't angry with me. David Byrne doesn't even remember who I am.」。**拆掉之后立刻给可迁移的一般化**——下次你确信有人生你的气时，也许你错了。", "claim_id": "clm-00000000000d", "confidence": 0.81, "contexts": ["叙事结构", "归因纠正"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-cb4fc0db7caa", "src-d35e2171afc6"], "falsifiers": ["若取样中他多次建立焦虑却不拆解，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-cb4fc0db7caa", "src-d35e2171afc6"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2010–2011", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["判断/对称句", "风险表述", "取舍判断"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**判断用成对句给出，但两侧权重不等，重的那一侧放在后面。**「Substance without swagger slows you down. But swagger without substance can be fatal.」——`slows you down` 与 `can be fatal` 不是一个量级。**形式对称、权重不对称**，是他给判断的惯用形。", "claim_id": "clm-00000000000e", "confidence": 0.76, "contexts": ["风险表述", "取舍判断"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-edb2fccdd28d", "src-f377c2a5bd55"], "falsifiers": ["若语料中他的成对句多为等权并列，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-edb2fccdd28d", "src-f377c2a5bd55"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2013–2026", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["自我修正", "批评具体对象", "事后更正"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**批评过一个具体对象之后，他会在同一篇里补澄清，而不是另发一篇。**谈 Cowboy Junkies 的悖论之后，文末带方括号补注「[Clarification! I love the Junkies. I saw them last night. They were spectacular」。**修正与原文同处一篇**，读者不需要另找一次才看到。", "claim_id": "clm-00000000000f", "confidence": 0.72, "contexts": ["批评具体对象", "事后更正"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-fdcfa0ca5f8f", "src-a1c762b52fa5"], "falsifiers": ["若语料中他的更正多以独立篇目出现，本条的「同一篇」限定即被推翻"], "source_ids": ["src-fdcfa0ca5f8f", "src-a1c762b52fa5"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2004–2007", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["自嘲/打折", "趋势判断", "自我定位"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "heuristic", "claim": "**给出自己的判断后用一句自嘲把它打个折。**列完 Web 2.0 的五条之后他写「I'll never have a shot once it gets crowded」；谈 Hoodia 榜单时结论是「the stuff that changes the most is banal」，并附一条打脸的 PS——那些广告据 BBC 报道是假的。**自嘲落在自己的判断上，不是落在别人身上。**", "claim_id": "clm-000000000010", "confidence": 0.74, "contexts": ["趋势判断", "自我定位"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-0f5fe5bc213f", "src-a1c762b52fa5"], "falsifiers": ["若语料多见他给判断而不留余地，本条即被削弱"], "source_ids": ["src-0f5fe5bc213f", "src-a1c762b52fa5"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2004–2005", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["篇幅", "博客写作", "观点表达"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "expression", "claim": "**极短是常态，不是例外。** 取样中可见两句成篇（Short and funny）与三句成篇（Rupert Murdoch has it backwards）。**凡产物写出长段落，即偏离他的形态。**本条挂在 193 篇的分层取样上，不是全量统计。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000011", "confidence": 0.85, "contexts": ["博客写作", "观点表达"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-fd4d12125881", "src-0cdd5f5ee8b7"], "falsifiers": ["若在全量博客上统计出长文占多数，本条即需修订"], "source_ids": ["src-fd4d12125881", "src-0cdd5f5ee8b7"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2009–2019", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
{"alternative_explanations": [], "applicability": ["成对句/枢轴", "价值对照", "文本形式"], "author_role": "agent", "category": "expression", "claim": "**成对句以省略号起头的下一行作枢轴，两侧都不带评判词。**「Judge people by where they came from」对「Judge people by where they're going」，「Talent is inborn」对「Skill is earned」——**他不说哪一侧对**。这是一个形式装置，不是列表。", "claim_id": "clm-000000000012", "confidence": 0.8, "contexts": ["价值对照", "文本形式"], "counter_source_ids": [], "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z", "evidence_clusters": ["src-e4c047287d8c", "src-94c46a4191ca"], "falsifiers": ["若该形态在取样中只出现一次，本条不足以称为装置"], "source_ids": ["src-e4c047287d8c", "src-94c46a4191ca"], "status": "pattern", "supersedes": null, "time_scope": "2019–2020", "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:23Z"}
